 @BassRacerx  me too.  but the thing i really hate about where i live is how hard it is to SELL my old stuff to upgrade. 


on ebay people can rip you off and say you sent rocks and ebay will side with them.  dont sell anything on ebay unless you can afford to lose it.


craigslist is ok but in a rural area you have people calling from 200 miles away.  and they want you to drive there or something

 @_Snapper  depends on what games you play, at what settings, and the refresh rate of your monitor.  if you live somewhere with a decent town size and can flip the 980 ti on craigslist then put that money into the 1080 ti, then sell the 1080 ti next year, then that might be the way to go.  


if the money wont bother you then go for it.  but if you gotta scrounge for cash then thats different


but like i said, whether the 980 ti will last depends on your settings,games,fp, refresh.

 @corbindaley2570  People buy what ever they want but facts are there for a reason.

The Red Devil has about the same temp as the 2070S, offers slighly less performance and as you said it worth 100$ less in your country.

Maybe for you spending those 100$ for what the 2070S offers to you makes sense, i dont know xD.
